{"event":"reply","n":1,"text":"Key details: words split on space only; the file may contain no other whitespace characters (just codes 32-126 and LF). Validation is per line in order, with errors taking precedence over output, so I parse everything first.\n\nRounding: for a non-negative value v and divisor d, (v*2+d)/(2d) in integer division gives round-half-up; apply the sign separately.\n\nTax rate: the format is 1-2 digits, \".\", 2 digits, \"%\". Value = digits without the dot, as hundredths of a percent. Discount: 1-3 digits then \"%\", with value ≤ 100 (e.g. \"0100%\" fails because it has 4 digits).\n\nQuantity: optional \"-\", then 1-3 digits. Price: 1-5 digits, \".\", 2 digits.\n\nMagnitudes fit in i64.\n\n\n<invoke name=\"none\">\n</invoke>\n```rust\nuse std::fs;\n\nfn rnd(v: i64, d: i64) -> i64 {\n    let s = if v < 0 { -1 } else { 1 };\n    let a = v.abs();\n    s * ((a * 2 + d) / (2 * d))\n}\n\nfn digits(s: &str, lo: usize, hi: usize) -> bool {\n    s.len() >= lo && s.len() <= hi && s.bytes().all(|c| c.is_ascii_digit())\n}\n\nfn fmt(c: i64) -> String {\n    let a = c.abs();\n    format!(\"{}{}.{:02}\", if c < 0 { \"-\" } else { \"\" }, a / 100, a % 100)\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();\n    let data = fs::read(&args[1]).unwrap();\n    let text = String::from_utf8_lossy(&data).to_string();\n    let mut out = String::new();\n    let (mut sn, mut st, mut stot) = (0i64, 0i64, 0i64);\n    let mut items = 0;\n    let mut lines: Vec<&str> = text.split('\\n').collect();\n    if let Some(l) = lines.last() {\n        if l.is_empty() {\n            lines.pop();\n        }\n    }\n    for (i, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n        let n = i + 1;\n        let w: Vec<&str> = line.split(' ').filter(|x| !x.is_empty()).collect();\n        if w.is_empty() {\n            continue;\n        }\n        let err = |m: &str| {\n            println!(\"error: line {}: {}\", n, m);\n            std::process::exit(20);\n        };\n        if w.len() != 5 {\n            err(&format!(\"expected 5 fields, got {}\", w.len()));\n        }\n        let name = w[0];\n        if !(name.len() >= 1\n            && name.len() <= 20\n            && name.bytes().all(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || c == b'_' || c == b'-'))\n        {\n            err(\"bad name\");\n        }\n        let q = w[1];\n        let (neg, qd) = if let Some(r) = q.strip_prefix('-') { (true, r) } else { (false, q) };\n        if !digits(qd, 1, 3) {\n            err(\"bad quantity\");\n        }\n        let mut qv: i64 = qd.parse().unwrap();\n        if neg {\n            qv = -qv;\n        }\n        let p = w[2];\n        let pb = p.as_bytes();\n        if !(p.len() >= 4\n            && p.len() <= 8\n            && pb[p.len() - 3] == b'.'\n            && digits(&p[..p.len() - 3], 1, 5)\n            && digits(&p[p.len() - 2..], 2, 2))\n        {\n            err(\"bad price\");\n        }\n        let pv: i64 = format!(\"{}{}\", &p[..p.len() - 3], &p[p.len() - 2..]).parse().unwrap();\n        let d = w[3];\n        if !(d.ends_with('%') && digits(&d[..d.len() - 1], 1, 3)) {\n            err(\"bad discount\");\n        }\n        let dv: i64 = d[..d.len() - 1].parse().unwrap();\n        if dv > 100 {\n            err(\"bad discount\");\n        }\n        let t = w[4];\n        let tb = t.as_bytes();\n        if !(t.ends_with('%')\n            && t.len() >= 6\n            && t.len() <= 7\n            && tb[t.len() - 4] == b'.'\n            && digits(&t[..t.len() - 4], 1, 2)\n            && digits(&t[t.len() - 3..t.len() - 1], 2, 2))\n        {\n            err(\"bad tax\");\n        }\n        let tv: i64 = format!(\"{}{}\", &t[..t.len() - 4], &t[t.len() - 3..t.len() - 1])\n            .parse()\n            .unwrap();\n        let gross = qv * pv;\n        let disc = rnd(gross * dv, 100);\n        let net = gross - disc;\n        let tax = rnd(net * tv, 10000);\n        let total = net + tax;\n        sn += net;\n        st += tax